WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.963
Last, what all this produces.

2
00:00:01.963 --> 00:00:06.425
During migration the program
classifies drift into five classes.

3
00:00:06.425 --> 00:00:11.337
Schema drift: an attribute encoding that
doesn't match the current schema version.

4
00:00:11.337 --> 00:00:13.802
Provenance drift: a state change with no

5
00:00:13.802 --> 00:00:16.863
provenance event in the
chain, which halts the run.

6
00:00:16.863 --> 00:00:21.813
Semantic drift: a value slipping back
into a deprecated naming pattern.

7
00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:25.007
Authorization drift: a
Conditional Access policy that

8
00:00:25.007 --> 00:00:28.549
contradicts the assurance level
recorded for the principal,.

9
00:00:28.549 --> 00:00:33.612
And identity drift: a principal in the
tenant with no counterpart in the registry.

10
00:00:33.612 --> 00:00:35.212
Be honest about maturity.

11
00:00:35.212 --> 00:00:39.387
Schema and provenance detection
are shipped, semantic is partial,

12
00:00:39.387 --> 00:00:43.106
and authorization and identity
detection are design-only;

13
00:00:43.106 --> 00:00:46.825
today, people reviewing the
assessment modules find those.

14
00:00:46.825 --> 00:00:51.224
From Phase 2 on, the agency can
produce an evidence bundle at any time:

15
00:00:51.224 --> 00:00:53.660
each phase's signed readiness bundle,

16
00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.352
both phase-tagged SPN
inventories and their comparison,

17
00:00:57.352 --> 00:01:00.651
the provenance chain for
every adapter operation,

18
00:01:00.651 --> 00:01:04.736
every drift finding with its
remediation, and the GCC boundary

19
00:01:04.736 --> 00:01:09.450
finding with its compensating controls
and when each was last verified.

20
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.813
Who reads it matters.

21
00:01:10.813 --> 00:01:13.513
FedRAMP authorizes
cloud service offerings,

22
00:01:13.513 --> 00:01:17.137
and third-party assessment
organizations assess providers.

23
00:01:17.137 --> 00:01:22.538
The agency's own system is authorized
by its authorizing official under the

24
00:01:22.538 --> 00:01:27.938
Risk Management Framework, SP 800-37,
which supports ongoing authorization.

25
00:01:27.938 --> 00:01:32.883
So the bundle goes to the security control
assessor and the authorizing official,

26
00:01:32.883 --> 00:01:36.301
as it happens, not assembled
over most of a year afterward.

27
00:01:36.301 --> 00:01:38.213
And it belongs to the agency.

28
00:01:38.213 --> 00:01:41.438
When the integrator leaves,
the registry, schemas,

29
00:01:41.438 --> 00:01:45.450
findings and evidence stay for
the next authorization cycle.

30
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:49.828
So, from Monday: start read-only
discovery with a pre-flight;

31
00:01:49.828 --> 00:01:53.295
turn the gaps into a
narrow, time-bound request;

32
00:01:53.295 --> 00:01:58.038
make every run evidence; and gate
every phase on its validation.

33
00:01:58.038 --> 00:02:03.587
Chapters 07 through 11 and the appendices
carry the full detail and the code.

34
00:02:03.587 --> 00:02:08.117
The Federal Modernization Workbook's
Book 03, HR-Driven Identity,

35
00:02:08.117 --> 00:02:11.388
picks up where the
attributes should come from.

36
00:02:11.388 --> 00:02:12.220
Thank you.
